"relationship": "related_topic",
"comparison": "Both MS and GS describe the general accounting treatment for AFS securities where unrealized losses are not driven by credit losses or intent to sell. MS specifies that for AFS securities 'not intended for sale,' the 'remainder of unrealized losses recognized in OCI' after isolating the credit loss. GS similarly states that 'unrealized fair value gains and losses are included in accumulated other comprehensive income/(loss)' for available-for-sale securities, implying that non-credit, non-sale-driven impairments flow through OCI. GS further clarifies in D195 that these unrealized losses are recorded in OCI, consistent with MS's separation of credit loss (earnings) from non-credit loss (OCI).",
