"relationship": "same_topic",
"comparison": "Both MS and JPM detail the split recognition of impairment for AFS securities that the firm intends to hold. MS recognizes the 'credit loss portion... in Other revenues' and the 'remainder... in OCI' for securities 'not intended for sale.' JPM mirrors this by stating that for securities the Firm has 'intent and ability to hold,' a credit loss is recognized as an 'allowance for credit losses' (earnings impact), while 'Any impairment... not due to credit losses is recorded in OCI.' Both policies distinguish between credit-driven losses (recognized in income/allowance) and non-credit impairments (recognized in OCI) for held securities.",
